[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Mad or Not?]
[00:01.30]Why do people think the writer is mad? | 为什么人们认为这位作者疯了？
[00:14.91]Aeroplanes are slowly driving me mad. | 飞机正慢慢地把我逼疯。
[00:20.08]I live near an airport and passing planes can be heard night and day. | 我住在一个机场附近，飞机从早到晚轰鸣而过。
[00:26.78]The airport was built years ago, but for some reason it could not be used then. | 机场是多年前修建的，但由于某种原因，那时无法投入使用。
[00:34.48]Last year, however, it came into use. | 然而，去年它投入使用了。
[00:39.21]Over a hundred people must have been driven away from their homes by the noise. | 一百多人一定是被噪音逼离了家园。
[00:46.08]I am one of the few people left. | 我是少数留下来的人之一。
[00:49.97]Sometimes I think this house will be knocked down by a passing plane. | 有时我想这房子会被一架路过的飞机撞倒。
[00:56.66]I have been offered a large sum of money to go away, but I am determined to stay here. | 有人给我一大笔钱让我搬走，但我决心留在这里。
[01:05.42]Everybody says I must be mad and they are probably right. | 大家都说我一定疯了，他们可能是对的。